", "upload": "image"}}, {"id": 123, "type": "MarkdownNote", "pos": [-1040, 0], "size": [500, 520], "flags": {}, "order": 2, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "title": "Note: Viggle Remake", "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "version": "7.8", "input_ue_unconnectable": {}}}, "widgets_values": ["## Viggle Remake - Character Swap\nSwap a person in your own video, keeping the motion and camera. Runs locally. This is not the Viggle app.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Source Video:** convert your clip to 24 fps first.\n2. **Pictures:** paint one to four frames of your clip with the new character. Any image editor works. These decide who appears.\n3. **Pins:** one source frame number per picture, in the same order, such as `72, 108`.\n4. **Frames:** must be 17n+5: 90, 107, 124, 141, 158, 175, 192, 209, 226, 243, 260, 277, 294. At 24 fps, 124 is about 5 s and 226 about 9 s. Timestamps in your prompt must fit.\n5. **Prompt:** six sections, describing the finished video, not the change. Viggle's PROMPTING.md explains them.\n6. **Sound:** the source audio carries over as long as it stays connected.\n\n**Switches:** turn Picture 3 and 4 on only when you use them, and add a pin for each one.\n\n**Tips:** full-body suits work better than non-human shapes. Throw away any painting where the pose changed. Test a short clip first.\n\n**Leave these alone:** Keyframe Until 0.9, sampler euler, Viggle's six swap sigmas.\n\nOnly use footage you have the right to change, and don't use real people who haven't agreed. MiniMax H3 Community License: read it before commercial use. Video by TheLocalLab: youtube.com/@TheLocalLab"], "widgets_values_named": {"text": "| megapixels | 2:3 portrait | 16:9 landscape |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.4 | 544 x 800 | 864 x 480 |\n| 0.6 | 640 x 960 | 1056 x 608 |\n| 0.8 | 736 x 1120 | 1216 x 672 |\n| 1.0 | 832 x 1248 | 1376 x 768 |\n| 1.2 | 928 x 1376 | 1504 x 832 |\n\n**VRAM:** 15 s with references ran out of memory at 1344x768 on 20 GB, and fit at 0.6 MP. Not measured with references on 12 or 16 GB.\nOutput (multiple=32). The RTX Video Super Resolution node doubles the final size."}, "color": "#222", "bgcolor": "#000"}, {"id": 124, "type": "MarkdownNote", "pos": [-520, 0], "size": [480, 300], "flags": {}, "order": 2, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "title": "Note: Model Links", "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "version": "7.8", "input_ue_unconnectable": {}}}, "widgets_values": ["## Model Links\n**Viggle swap model** (Viggle) - https://huggingface.co/Viggle/Viggle-Remake/tree/main/int8\n- viggle_remake_swap_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors (~21 GB) -> ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/\n- The swap is already built in. Don't add a LoRA on top.\n\n**Text encoder and VAEs** - https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/tree/main\n- qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors (~16 GB) -> models/text_encoders/\n- minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors, minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors -> models/vae/\n\n**Viggle node pack** - https://huggingface.co/Viggle/Viggle-Remake/tree/main/comfyui/ComfyUI-Viggle-Remake\n- Copy the ComfyUI-Viggle-Remake folder to ComfyUI/custom_nodes/, then restart.\n\nUse PyTorch built for CUDA 13 (cu130) with driver 580+."], "widgets_values_named": {"text": "| megapixels | 2:3 portrait | 16:9 landscape |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.4 | 544 x 800 | 864 x 480 |\n| 0.6 | 640 x 960 | 1056 x 608 |\n| 0.8 | 736 x 1120 | 1216 x 672 |\n| 1.0 | 832 x 1248 | 1376 x 768 |\n| 1.2 | 928 x 1376 | 1504 x 832 |\n\n**VRAM:** 15 s with references ran out of memory at 1344x768 on 20 GB, and fit at 0.6 MP. Not measured with references on 12 or 16 GB.\nOutput (multiple=32). The RTX Video Super Resolution node doubles the final size."}, "color": "#222", "bgcolor": "#000"}, {"id": 125, "type": "MarkdownNote", "pos": [-520, 320], "size": [480, 300], "flags": {}, "order": 2, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "title": "Note: Tested Numbers", "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "version": "7.8", "input_ue_unconnectable": {}}}, "widgets_values": ["**Measured on an RTX 4000 Ada (20 GB), PyTorch cu130, 832x480, sampling time:**\n- 124 frames (5 s): 2:51\n- 175 frames (7 s): 4:55\n- 226 frames (9 s): 7:21. On cu128: 13:52.\n- 294 frames (12 s): 11:58.\n\n**VRAM caps on this card, a simulation, not real smaller cards.** 226 frames stayed inside a 16 GB cap (peak 15.8 GB) and a 12 GB cap (peak 11.9 GB), at the same speed, with the same output.\n\nSystem RAM reached about 50 GB in these runs.\n\nThe VSA gate crashed on this model, so leave it out."], "widgets_values_named": {"text": "| megapixels | 2:3 portrait | 16:9 landscape |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.4 | 544 x 800 | 864 x 480 |\n| 0.6 | 640 x 960 | 1056 x 608 |\n| 0.8 | 736 x 1120 | 1216 x 672 |\n| 1.0 | 832 x 1248 | 1376 x 768 |\n| 1.2 | 928 x 1376 | 1504 x 832 |\n\n**VRAM:** 15 s with references ran out of memory at 1344x768 on 20 GB, and fit at 0.6 MP. Not measured with references on 12 or 16 GB.\nOutput (multiple=32). The RTX Video Super Resolution node doubles the final size."}, "color": "#222", "bgcolor": "#000"}, {"id": 126, "type": "Fast Groups Muter (rgthree)", "pos": [0, 500], "size": [300, 220], "flags": {}, "order": 6, "mode": 0, "inputs": [], "outputs": [{"name": "OPT_CONNECTION", "type": "*", "links": null}], "title": "Pictures", "properties": {"matchColors": "", "matchTitle": "Picture", "showNav": true, "showAllGraphs": true, "sort": "position", "customSortAlphabet": "", "toggleRestriction": "default"}, "color": "#222", "bgcolor": "#000"}], "links": [[2, 1, 0, 3, 0, "MODEL"], [3, 7, 0, 8, 0, "VIDEO"], [4, 4, 0, 11, 0, "CLIP"], [5, 5, 0, 11, 1, "VAE"], [6, 6, 0, 11, 2, "VAE"], [7, 8, 0, 11, 3, "IMAGE"], [8, 8, 1, 11, 5, "AUDIO"], [9, 9, 0, 11, 4, "IMAGE"], [10, 10, 0, 11, 6, "IMAGE"], [11, 11, 0, 12, 0, "CONDITIONING"], [12, 3, 0, 13, 0, "MODEL"], [13, 11, 0, 13, 1, "CONDITIONING"], [14, 12, 0, 16, 0, "NOISE"], [15, 13, 0, 16, 1, "GUIDER"], [16, 14, 0, 16, 2,